    "outcome": "success",
    "answer": "The task cards in `QueuePanel.axaml` use a `Border.queueCard` (which has `CornerRadius=\"8\"` from the theme) with visual properties bound to `TaskRowViewModel`. The current issues are:\n\n1. **Square edges**: The `selectionRail` inside the card has `CornerRadius=\"8,0,0,8\"` (left side only), leaving the right side square. Combined with the outer `Grid` container's square corners, this creates a squared-off visual despite the `queueCard`'s rounded corners.\n\n2. **Combined active+in-progress state is broken**: When a card is both `IsSelected` (blue, active) and `IsRunning` (green, in-progress), the `BorderBrush` property prioritizes `IsRunning` \u2014 the blue selected border is completely hidden. The task wants an outer blue border + inner green border when both states apply.\n\n3. **Rounded corners for all states**: Need to ensure default, active (selected/blue), in-progress (running/green), and the combined state all have consistent rounded corners with no square edges.\n\n**Files to touch:**\n- `QueuePanel.axaml` \u2014 card template\n- `TaskRowViewModel.cs` \u2014 visual property computation\n- Possibly `VisualRelayTheme.axaml` \u2014 theme style adjustments\n\n```json\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Task cards in the queue list have three issues: (1) the selectionRail has square right edges and the outer container introduces square visual artifacts \u2014 we need rounded corners uniformly; (2) the combined active+in-progress state (IsSelected + IsRunning) is currently invisible because IsRunning overrides IsSelected in the BorderBrush ternary, but the task calls for an outer blue border around the green inner border when both are true; (3) all four states (default, selected, running, combined) must have consistent rounded corners. The template lives in QueuePanel.axaml (lines 60-129) with computed visual properties from TaskRowViewModel.cs (lines 90-97).\",\n  \"options\": [\n    \"Nested-Border approach: Replace the single Border.queueCard with two stacked Borders \u2014 the outer one showing the blue selected highlight (BorderBrush=SelectedBorderBrush, larger CornerRadius) and the inner one showing the green running highlight plus the card content. Both use full CornerRadius='8'. The selectionRail gets CornerRadius='8,0,0,8' but is kept inside the inner Border. The ViewModel gets a combined-state flag (IsRunning && IsSelected) to toggle a third visual tier.\",\n    \"BoxShadow + thickness trick: Keep a single Border but when combined, use a blue BoxShadow to simulate an outer blue glow/border around the green border. Fix the selectionRail to use CornerRadius='8,0,0,8' (already) but clip it properly so its square right edge is hidden. Add a combined shadow constant in the ViewModel.\",\n    \"Overlay Grid approach: Wrap the card content in a Grid with two overlapping Border layers \u2014 the top layer is transparent with a blue border (for selected), the bottom layer has a green border (for running). Opacity toggles based on the combined state. Fix selectionRail and ensure all CornerRadius values are uniform at 8px across all states.\"\n  ]\n}\n```",
    "exit_code": 0
  },
